# Migration safety scanner — acknowledged intentional-risk migrations.
#
# `bun run db:migration-safety` scans `migration.sql` files for
# destructive operations (DROP TABLE, DROP COLUMN, ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE,
# ADD COLUMN ... NOT NULL without DEFAULT). Migrations listed here have
# been reviewed and intentionally accepted, so the scanner emits an `INFO:`
# (acknowledged) line instead of `WARN:` for those findings — `doctor` then
# stays quiet about already-reviewed history while still surfacing new
# destructive operations loudly.
#
# Format
#   <migration_dir_name>  <freeform reason>
#
# Rules
#   - One acknowledged migration per non-blank, non-comment line.
#   - Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.
#   - The migration name is the directory name under
#     `packages/server/prisma/migrations/` (e.g.
#     `20260408223838_convert_string_fields_to_enums`).
#   - Reason text after the first whitespace is shown alongside the INFO
#     line. Keep it short and specific (what was reviewed, why it's safe to
#     apply once).
#
# Adding an entry is a deliberate review signal. Only acknowledge a
# migration after confirming the destructive operation has the dependent
# code/data changes it needs (backfill landed, dependent reads removed,
# downtime/coordination plan agreed). New destructive migrations should be
# reviewed and acknowledged at PR time, not silently after the fact.

20260408223838_convert_string_fields_to_enums  Reviewed: ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE narrowings of spells/equipment/magic-items text columns to enums; USING cast covers existing rows.
